<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/harness/server/retained',
        '/harness/server/closures',
        '/harness/gate/in-a-fresh-process',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/harness/tests/server.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('allocated() comes back tagged, with its rep count and its growth'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Price what parsing an invoice link allocates">
        <p>The body runs <code>reps</code> times, 1000 by default, and <code>perRep</code> is
            the mean by engine type. A fraction means the allocation is conditional or
            amortized.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { allocated } from '@abide/harness/server'

            const answer = allocated(() => new URL('https://crm.test/invoices/42'), 400)
            answer.tagged // 'batch mean'
            answer.perRep // objects per run, by type
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Check the cost per run holds across the batch">
        <p>The batch is split in two, and <code>growth</code> is the second half's mean minus
            the first's. A type left out of it cost the same in both halves.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            const answer = allocated(() => new URL('https://crm.test/invoices/42'))
            answer.growth // {} when every run costs the same
        `} />
        <p>Gate an exact count on <code>retained</code>. A mean is not a count to compare
            with <code>toBe</code>.</p>
    </Section>
</Doc>
